        <guid>https://www.vanguardrenewables.com/latest/sustainable-manure-management-for-small-dairy-farms-the-challenges-and-a-farm-pow</guid>
        <pubDate>Thu, 11 Jul 2024 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <description><![CDATA[Manure management is a critical aspect of sustainable agriculture, particularly for smaller dairy farms where resources and space are limited. Methane, a greenhouse gas that is a leading cause of climate change, is released when manure is stored in open lagoons and land applied on the farm’s fields. According to the Environmental Defense Fund (EDF), “Livestock - primarily beef and dairy cows – account for the vast majority of agriculture methane emissions,” which is why organizations like the EDF are working to help farmers mitigate as much methane as possible. ]]></description>
        
        <enclosure url="https://www.datocms-assets.com/97698/1701381557-slide-clean-energy.png?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;fit=clamp&amp;q=70" type="image/jpeg" />
